VERSION             "1"
CONFIG              ""
FILENOTES           ""

// Overrides of STOCK engine strings (the game's own zone ships these; a copy baked
// into mod.ff wins). A localized asset is named <STR FILENAME>_<REFERENCE>, so the
// engine's CGAME_* strings MUST live in cgame.str - the same entries in gf.str would
// compile to GF_* and be read by nothing. Verified: an EMPTY value renders as nothing
// (the engine does not fall back to printing the raw key).
//
// Keep overrides to single-purpose keys. The scoreboard's other columns come from
// MPUI_* (KILLS/DEATHS/ASSISTS/...), which are ALSO used by the combat record,
// leaderboards and after-action report - renaming one changes it everywhere in the
// client UI, not just the scoreboard.

// Score in Gunfight IS cumulative damage dealt (gf_onPlayerDamage), so the stock
// "Score" header actively misleads. CGAME_SB_SCORE is scoreboard-scoped, so this
// rename is contained.
REFERENCE           SB_SCORE
LANG_ENGLISH        "Damage"

// Blanks the "Connection Interrupted" banner TEXT. It is drawn by client engine code
// (CG_DrawDisconnect) and there is NO dvar to disable it - the client has no
// cg_drawDisconnect - so blanking its localized string is the only lever on the text
// (the plug ICON still renders and cannot be removed; see [[modff-cannot-embed-new-images]]).
// ⚠ HISTORY, corrected: an earlier version of this comment called the banner "the
// irreducible floor of native SD round cycling". That framing is RETIRED - GF_ENDTL
// measured dark=0ms (the server never goes snapshot-silent between rounds), and the plug
// players actually saw was the FINAL-KILLCAM timescale dilation starving the usercmd ack
// rate: a real server-side cause, FIXED by the scr_gf_killcam_slowmo floor (0.6, shipped
// 2026-07-13; [[killcam-slowmo-timescale-usercmd-backlog]]). This blank stays only as
// cosmetic cover for GENUINE lag - never cite it as evidence a symptom is unfixable.
// TRADE-OFF: it ALSO suppresses the warning for genuine lag / packet loss.
REFERENCE           CONNECTIONINTERUPTED
LANG_ENGLISH        ""

ENDMARKER
